# What `railway up` must never upload.
#
# `railway up` tarballs this directory and sends it to the builder. Whether it
# honours .gitignore is not something to find out by testing it against
# production, so the personal-data paths are repeated here explicitly. The
# service reads none of these at runtime — production storage is Postgres, and
# refuseToStartIfStorageContradictsTheNotice enforces that — so excluding them
# costs nothing and keeps homeowner records out of a built image.
#
# Keep in step with .gitignore. Anything protected there belongs here too.

# Captured homeowner leads and detection logs.
data/*.jsonl
data/usage.json

# Real surveyed properties — contains addresses.
data/survey-samples.json

# Lead delivery records — billing evidence, and homeowner details.
data/deliveries.jsonl
data/delivery-failures.jsonl

# Stored renders — photorealistic images of identified homes.
data/renders/

# Database dumps. Every row, including homeowners.
backup-*.json
*.backup.json

# Local environment and build noise.
.env
.env.local
node_modules/
